loss":"saying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பாண்கடன்","parts":[{"text":"பாண்","lemma":"பாண்","gloss":"bards"},{"text":"கடன்","lemma":"கடன்","gloss":"duty"}],"gloss":"duty to the bards"},{"surface":"இறுக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"இறுக்கும்","lemma":"இறு","gloss":"paying/fulfilling"}],"gloss":"fulfilling"},{"surface":"வள்ளியோய்","parts":[{"text":"வள்ளியோய்","lemma":"வள்ளல்","gloss":"O generous one"}],"gloss":"O generous one"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பூண்கடன்","parts":[{"text":"பூண்","lemma":"பூண்","gloss":"undertaken"},{"text":"கடன்","lemma":"கடன்","gloss":"duty"}],"gloss":"undertaken duty"},{"surface":"எந்தை","parts":[{"text":"எந்தை","lemma":"எந்தை","gloss":"my lord/father"}],"gloss":"my lord"},{"surface":"நீ","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"இரவலர்","parts":[{"text":"இரவலர்","lemma":"இரவலர்","gloss":"supplicants"}],"gloss":"supplicants"},{"surface":"புரவே","parts":[{"text":"புரவு","lemma":"புர","gloss":"protecting"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed protecting"}]}],"literal":"That which passed having rained, even if the sky fails / even if the earth hides its fertility, saying the old yield is gone / without support, for all living beings, existence / \"give us more,\" if people like us beg / \"you already received before,\" if people like you refuse / that is painful indeed, O lord of the well-made chariot! / Even more than those who are unable to fill what is lacking, / those who come seeking and lose their hope [are to be pitied]. / You are not such a person, you! Even when enemies' / difficult fortresses belong to them, saying \"it is yours\" / O generous one who fulfills the duty to the bards! / Protecting the supplicants is your undertaken duty, my lord!","translation":"Even if the sky fails to rain as it did before, and even if the earth hides its fertility saying the old yield is gone, life is impossible for all living beings without support. In such times, if people like us beg, saying 'give us more,' and if people like you refuse, saying 'you have already received before,' that is painful indeed, O lord of the well-made chariot! More than those who are unable to relieve the poverty of others, those who come seeking with hope and go away disappointed are truly to be pitied. But you are not such a person! Even when the difficult fortresses of your enemies still belong to them, you declare 'they are yours' and fulfill your duty to the bards, O generous one! Protecting the supplicants is the duty you have undertaken, my lord!","modern":"மழை பொழிவது நின்று மேகம் பொய்த்தாலும், பழைய விளைச்சல் முடிந்துவிட்டது என்று பூமி தன் வளத்தை மறைத்துக் கொண்டாலும், உலகத்து உயிர்கள் அனைத்தும் கொடையாளிகள் இல்லாமல் வாழ முடியாது. அப்படிப்பட்ட வறுமைக் காலத்தில், எங்களைப் போன்ற இரவலர்கள் 'இன்னும் தாருங்கள்' என்று இரந்து கேட்கும்போது, உங்களைப் போன்ற வள்ளல்கள் 'முன்னரே பெற்றுக்கொண்டீர்களே' என்று கூறி மறுப்பது மிகவும் துன்பம் தருவதாகும், இயங்கும் தேரையுடைய தலைவனே! வறுமையைப் போக்க இயலாதவர்களை விட, நம்பி வந்த இரவலர்கள் ஏமாற்றமடைந்து திரும்புவதே பெரும் துன்பமாகும். நீயோ அப்படிப்பட்டவன் அல்லை. பகைவர்களின் அரிய கோட்டைகள் இன்னும் அவர்கள் வசமிருக்கும் போதே, 'இவை உங்களுடையவை' என்று பாணர்களுக்குக் கொடுத்துத் தன் கடமையைச் செய்யும் வள்ளல் நீ! இரவலர்களைக் காப்பதே என் தந்தையாகிய நீ பூண்ட கடமையாகும்.","explanation":"The poet Ūṉpoti Pacuṅkuṭaiyār addresses the Chera king Neytalaṅkāṉal Iḷañcēṭ Ceṉṉi, praising his extraordinary generosity. He begins by describing a severe drought where both the sky and the earth fail to yield. In such times, when supplicants beg for more, it is deeply painful if patrons refuse them by saying they have already given before. The poet notes that worse than being unable to give is causing a hopeful seeker to leave disappointed. The king, however, is so generous that he gifts away enemy fortresses to bards even before fully conquering them. Protecting the needy is presented as the king's ultimate undertaken duty.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.4],[1.4,1.9],[1.9,2.6],[2.6,3.3],[3.3,3.7],[3.7,4.4],[4.4,4.6],[4.6,5.8],[5.8,6.1],[6.1,6.3],[6.3,6.6],[6.6,7.14],[7.14,7.69],[7.69,8.36],[8.36,9.04],[9.04,9.59],[9.59,10.4],[10.4,11.08],[11.08,11.76],[11.76,12.3],[12.3,12.5],[12.5,12.8],[12.8,13.2],[13.2,13.78],[13.78,14.5],[14.5,14.8],[14.8,15.5],[15.5,15.8],[15.8,16.1],[16.1,16.4],[16.4,16.7],[18.36,18.96],[18.96,19.26],[19.26,19.56],[19.56,19.76],[20.32,21.06],[21.06,21.76],[21.76,22.16],[22.16,22.46],[22.46,23.4],[23.4,23.88],[23.88,24.36],[25.66,26.31],[26.31,26.72],[26.72,26.96],[26.96,27.26],[27.26,27.56]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.5],[1.5,2.0],[2.0,2.55],[2.55,3.11],[3.11,3.8],[3.8,4.6],[4.6,4.8],[4.8,6.2],[6.2,6.6],[6.6,6.8],[6.8,7.0],[7.0,7.63],[7.63,8.26],[8.26,9.05],[9.05,9.84],[9.84,10.47],[10.47,11.41],[11.41,12.2],[12.2,12.6],[12.6,13.29],[13.29,13.8],[13.8,14.2],[14.2,14.6],[14.6,15.04],[15.04,15.6],[15.6,16.0],[16.0,16.58],[16.7,17.34],[17.34,17.5],[17.5,18.43],[18.43,18.8],[19.6,20.3],[20.3,20.7],[20.7,21.2],[21.2,21.5],[21.5,23.1],[23.1,23.8],[24.01,24.3],[24.3,24.7],[24.7,25.2],[25.2,25.95],[25.95,26.7],[26.7,27.78],[27.78,28.26],[28.26,28.54],[28.54,29.11],[29.11,29.4]]},"sync":[[["கழிந்தது","that which has passed"]],[["பொழிந்தது","rained"],["என","as/saying"]],[["வான்","sky/cloud"],["கண்","place/source"]],[["மாறினும்","even if it fails"]],[["தொல்லது","old/customary yield"]],[["விளைந்து","having yielded"],["என","as/saying"]],[["நிலம்","earth"],["வளம்","fertility"]],[["கரப்பினும்","even if it hides"]],[["எல்லா","all"]],[["உயிர்க்கும்","to all living beings"]],[["இல்லால்","if there is not"]],[["வாழ்க்கை","life"]],[["இன்னும்","still/more"]],[["தம்","give to them"],["என","saying"]],[["எம்ம்னோர்","people like us"]],[["இரப்பின்","if they beg"]],[["முன்னும்","even before"]],[["கொண்டிர்","you received"],["என","saying"]],[["நும்மனோர்","people like you"]],[["மறுத்தல்","refusing"]],[["இன்னாது","is painful"]],[["அம்ம","alas"]],[["இயல்","well-made"],["தேர்","chariot"]],[["அண்ணல்","O lord"]],[["இல்லது",